---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CardGrid from '../../../components/CardGrid.astro';
import DocCard from '../../../components/DocCard.astro';
const sidebar = [
  { title: 'Documentation Home', href: '/docs' },
  { title: 'Reference Overview', href: '/docs/reference' },
  { title: 'Glossary', href: '/docs/reference/glossary' },
  { title: 'Known Issues', href: '/docs/reference/known-issues', active: true },
  { title: 'Roadmap', href: '/docs/reference/roadmap' },
  { title: 'Changelog', href: '/docs/reference/changelog' },
  { title: 'Literature', href: '/docs/reference/literature' },
];
const toc = [
  { id: 'issues', text: 'Known Issues', level: 2 },
  { id: 'corrections', text: 'Corrections', level: 2 },
  { id: 'reporting', text: 'Reporting', level: 2 },
];
---
<DocsLayout title="Known Issues & Corrections" description="Known issues and their corrections or workarounds" section="Reference" sidebar={sidebar} toc={toc}>
  <CardGrid columns={3}>
    <DocCard title="Dashboard drift" icon="chart" tag="Current" description="Offline and live dashboard state can diverge. Rebuild to NDJSON or export the live objects." meta="Workaround" />
    <DocCard title="Same-host Suricata" icon="network" tag="Current" description="Loopback capture can attribute alerts to container-internal addresses, so reputation may not fire locally." meta="Test externally" />
    <DocCard title="Timeline auth" icon="eye" tag="Current" description="Embed-mode capture needs a Kibana login; configure autologin or use a manual session." meta="Setup" />
    <DocCard title="fast.log parser" icon="file" tag="Historical" description="Eight capture groups into seven variables shifted fields silently. Replaced by structured eve.json." meta="Fixed" />
    <DocCard title="admin-ajax false positives" icon="alert" tag="Historical" description="A blanket admin-ajax rule flagged normal traffic. It is now excluded and analysed separately." meta="Fixed" />
    <DocCard title="Session laundering" icon="fingerprint" tag="Historical" description="A single clean request could reset a risky session. Score accumulation now prevents it." meta="Fixed" />
  </CardGrid>

  <h2 id="issues">Known Issues</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Dashboard generation drift:</strong> Offline vs live dashboard state can diverge. Workaround: Re-run build_dashboards.py --ndjson or export_dashboards.py.</li>
    <li><strong>Timeline capture requires Kibana auth:</strong> Configure autologin scripts or manual login.</li>
    <li><strong>Suricata same-host testing misattributes src_ip:</strong> Suricata runs with network_mode: host. In same-host test setups, alert src_ip may be container-internal. Workaround: is_private_ip() filters RFC1918/loopback at ingestion.</li>
    <li><strong>Fast.log regex parsing bug (historical):</strong> 8 capture groups into 7 variables shifted all fields. Fixed by switching to structured eve.json.</li>
    <li><strong>Admin-ajax.php false positives (historical):</strong> Blanket-flagged every admin-ajax.php request. Fixed: excluded from is_admin_access(), gets dedicated analysis.</li>
    <li><strong>Session score laundering (historical):</strong> Single clean request reset CVE-triggered sessions. Fixed by score accumulation in router.lua.</li>
    <li><strong>is_vulnerable_plugin_request() hyphen-escaping bug (historical):</strong> Un-escaped plugin slug broke match for hyphenated slugs. Fixed via lua_pattern_utils.escape_pattern().</li>
    <li><strong>ngx.null sentinel crash (historical):</strong> red:get() returns ngx.null userdata for missing key. Fixed with if not raw or raw == ngx.null idiom.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="corrections">Corrections</h2>
  <p>Corrections to documentation should be recorded here with issue references and resolution notes.</p>

  <h2 id="reporting">Reporting</h2>
  <p>New known issues should be added with severity, affected versions, and workarounds.</p>
</DocsLayout>
